content.text:
In-place list filtering that skips elements. Save /workspace/moderation.py:

BANNED = {"spam", "scam"}

def remove_banned(words):
    # remove banned words from the list in place and return it
    for w in words:
        if w in BANNED:
            words.remove(w)
    return words

Mutating a list while iterating skips the element after each removal, so consecutive banned words survive: remove_banned(['spam','scam','ok']) leaves 'scam' in place. Write tests/test_moderation.py first with that case plus ['spam','spam','spam'] -> [] and ['ok','spam','fine'] -> ['ok','fine'], run pytest, confirm the survivors. Then fix while KEEPING the in-place contract (callers hold references to the same list object): use slice assignment words[:] = [w for w in words if w not in BANNED] and add a test asserting the returned object IS the object passed in. Also parametrize a dozen mixed cases; finish with pytest green.

